  "narrative": "The residual-marker sweep gives a mostly negative picture except for feature_063. For feature_060, the full marginal Welch contrast R51 is tiny and imprecise around zero in both registered directions (H34 signed -0.0126; interval -0.0922 to +0.0671; H84 signed +0.0126; interval -0.0671 to +0.0922). The joint top-negative-stratum test R54 is also essentially null (H87 signed +0.0005; interval -0.0536 to +0.0547; H88 signed -0.0005; interval -0.0547 to +0.0536). For feature_035, the full marginal test R52 is near zero (H82 signed +0.0107; interval -0.0717 to +0.0930; H83 signed -0.0107; interval -0.0930 to +0.0717), and the top-negative-stratum test R53 is small and imprecise (H85 signed -0.0343; interval -0.0936 to +0.0251; H86 signed +0.0343; interval -0.0251 to +0.0936). I reject and close feature_060 and feature_035 in all tested contexts because none provides evidence of an association even approaching the 0.15-unit practical threshold.\n\nThe feature_003-by-feature_040 interaction is also null: R56 gives H91 signed -0.0339 (interval -0.1920 to +0.1241) and H92 signed +0.0339 (interval -0.1241 to +0.1920). This does not support the hypothesis that the borderline feature_003 association is substantially modified by log progression-free survival strata. I reject both interaction directions. This does not change the borderline feature_003 main-effect evidence, which remains unresolved and deferred because its point estimates were just below the practical threshold.\n\nThe new candidate is feature_063. The signed negative-direction test H90, R55, is +0.2268 with a 95% interval from +0.1307 to +0.3229 and cell sizes 266 versus 1734. Because H90 direction is -1, this corresponds to a raw mean difference of approximately -0.227 composite units for feature_063=1 versus feature_063=0: feature_063 positivity is associated with a more negative composite dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency, in this supplied dataset. The opposite registered direction H89 is inconsistent with this pattern and is rejected. The point estimate exceeds the 0.15-unit threshold and the interval strongly excludes zero, so this is the strongest newly discovered residual marker so far.\n\nHowever, I do not accept H90 yet as a final conclusion. The lower confidence bound (+0.1307) is still below the practical threshold, so the data do not decisively establish that the true marginal effect exceeds 0.15 units. Moreover, this is an unadjusted marginal contrast after many binary-marker contrasts, so multiplicity remains a concern. It is also unclear whether feature_063 is partially correlated with the validated core markers feature_037, feature_002, or feature_010; a marginal association need not be independent of them. I therefore leave H90 unresolved but active and request independent validation. If validation confirms a precise threshold-exceeding association, the next step is to determine whether the association persists in the joint core-negative stratum and whether it is modified by the strongest core marker feature_037; the newly registered feature_063 refinements are aimed at that follow-up. All assessments remain associations within this supplied dataset, not causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Validated core dataset-specific main associations: H19 feature_037=1 -> more negative outcome_001/stronger dependency, about 0.82-0.83 units; H24 feature_002=1 -> less negative outcome_001/weaker dependency, about 0.77-0.83 units; H16 feature_010=1 -> less negative outcome_001/weaker dependency, about 0.35-0.42 units. Interaction map: no supported feature_037-by-feature_002, no supported feature_037-by-feature_010, no robust feature_002-by-feature_010 after validation, no feature_010-by-feature_040. H64 feature_002-by-feature_040 remains borderline positive (+0.153, lower +0.022), unresolved/deferred. New residual-marker results: feature_035 null marginal and top-negative; feature_060 null marginal and top-negative; feature_001 null; feature_003 remains borderline below-threshold positive for negative-direction (weaker? actually stronger dependency) main effects and null feature_040 interaction. H90 feature_063=1 -> stronger dependency candidate, signed +0.227 (interval +0.131 to +0.323) for direction -1; opposite direction H89 rejected. H90 is unresolved active pending validation. Requested validation: H90. Follow-up refinements registered: feature_063 effect in joint core-negative stratum (H93), in feature_037=0 and =1 strata (H94/H95), and feature_063-by-feature_037 interactions both directions (H96/H97). Interpretation remains dataset-specific association, not causality or generalizability.",
